# What `docker build` must never send to the daemon. The build context is the
# repository root (docker-compose.yml sets `context: ../../..`), and the image
# copies all of src/lasagna/, which is where src/lasagna/deploy/README.md tells
# operators to put .env with the JWT secret, the Postgres password and API keys.
# Without this file that .env was baked into every image layer.
#
# Docker reads these patterns relative to the context root; `**/` matches any
# depth and the last matching line wins. tests/test_docker_build_context.py
# checks the rules below with the same matching Docker uses.

# Secrets and local configuration, at any depth. The example file stays: it is
# documentation and holds no values.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.secrets.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
**/gha-creds-*.json
**/.pypirc
**/.npmrc

# The Kubernetes manifests. Nothing in the image reads them, and an operator's
# secrets live there: in overlays/local/ (src/lasagna/deploy/README.md,
# "Kubernetes"), or in base/secrets.yaml itself, which the README used to say
# to edit in place.
src/lasagna/deploy/k8s

# Version control and virtual environments
.git
.venv*
**/venv
**/env

# Build output (the root only: src/lasagna/configurator/frontend/dist is the
# built UI the package ships) and caches
build
dist
**/*.egg-info
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.hypothesis

# Test and run artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov
e2e/reports
**/rag_uploads
**/uploads
**/dbs
**/*.db
**/*.milvus.db
**/*.sqlite
